    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Rhanna is a charming three-bedroom detached bungalow set on approximately 0.4 acres of mature private grounds in the peaceful countryside of Cornamucklagh, Broadford, Co. Kildare. Presented in excellent condition throughout, this attractive home combines character, comfort and excellent potential for future expansion.\n\nExtending to approximately 107 sq. m, the property offers bright and well-appointed accommodation comprising a kitchen/dining area, sunroom, comfortable lounge, three bedrooms and family bathroom. The well-appointed country-style kitchen is a particular feature of the home, with a beautiful Rangemaster range cooker forming an impressive centrepiece. The adjoining sunroom provides a bright additional living space overlooking the gardens, while the lounge offers a warm and inviting setting with its attractive feature fireplace.\n\nExternally, the property is approached through a private gated entrance onto a generous gravel driveway and is surrounded by mature hedging, established trees and beautifully maintained gardens, providing excellent privacy. A substantial detached garage provides excellent storage and workshop space.\n\nA major feature of Rhanna is the benefit of full planning permission for a substantial two-storey extension to the rear, offering an exciting opportunity to significantly increase the existing accommodation Ideally situated in the countryside at Cornamucklagh, Broadford, the property enjoys a tranquil rural setting while remaining within easy reach of Broadford, Edenderry, Enfield and surrounding towns.\n\nConvenient access to the M4 motorway at Enfield provides excellent connectivity to Dublin City and the wider commuter network, combining peaceful country living with excellent accessibility.\n\nACCOMMODATION\n\nEntrance Hall\nWith tiled flooring and hardwood front door.\n\nLounge-14'7\" x 9'1\"\nWith wooden flooring, ceiling coving and centrepiece, open fire with marble fireplace and tiled hearth and TV point.\n\nKitchen/Dining Room-28'8\" x 10'5\"\nWith wooden flooring, solid wood built in wall to floor units, quartz countertop and upstand, tiled splashback, Belfast style sink, rangmaster cooker with gas hobs, dishwasher and door to front driveway.\n\nSunroom-14'5\" x 10'6\"\nWith wooden flooring, solid fuel stove and French doors to rear patio.\n\nBedroom 1-14'7\" x 9'9\"\nWith wooden flooring and built in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 2-12'4\" x 9'4\"\nWith wooden flooring.\n\nBedroom 3-8'3\" x 6'4\"\nWith wooden flooring.\n\nBathroom-7'6\" x 6'8\"\nWith tiled flooring, free standing bath, w.h.b and w.c.\n\nFIXTURES & FITTINGS\n\nAll flooring, curtains, blinds, light fittings (excluding sunroom), rangemaster and dishwasher are included in the sale.\n\nFEATURES\n\n• Presented in excellent condition throughout\n• Three-bedroom detached bungalow extending to c. 107 sq. m\n• Site extending to c. 0.4 acres\n• Substantial detached garage\n• Full planning permission for a significant twostorey rear extension\n• Mature, landscaped gardens and private grounds\n• Well-appointed kitchen with impressive Rangemaster range cooker\n• Bright sunroom overlooking the gardens\n• Private gated entrance with generous gravel driveway\n• Peaceful rural location with convenient access to Enfield, Edenderry and the M4 motorway\n\nDIRECTIONS\n\nEIRCODE: W91 WC6H"
      },
